// Waivers for the lint-only run in `make lint`.
//
// Careful: no comment line in here may start with the tool's own name. Its
// preprocessor reads that as a pragma and fails with BADVLTPRAGMA.
//
// Same two warnings the cocotb build switches off (-Wno-DECLFILENAME
// -Wno-UNUSEDSIGNAL in verif/cocotb/Makefile), so lint and sim agree.
//
// The glob is "*rtl/*.sv" rather than "*/rtl/*.sv". make lint passes
// relative paths like rtl/foo.sv, with no slash in front of rtl, so the
// second form never matches. Checked on 5.051-devel.
`verilator_config
lint_off -rule DECLFILENAME -file "*rtl/*.sv"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*rtl/*.sv"
